    <!-- ANNOTATION -->
    <mxCell id="INSIGHT" value="&lt;font color=&quot;#ff0000&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Architecture Bottleneck Insight:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;Scale Proportions&lt;/b&gt;: This diagram is drawn to &lt;b&gt;exact scale&lt;/b&gt; (~6,666 cycles/px). Notice how the Memory Interface &lt;i&gt;LOAD_ROW&lt;/i&gt; (7,686 cycles, 2px wide) is completely dwarfed by the Compute Engine &lt;i&gt;UpConv_Fused_Row&lt;/i&gt; (2,877,630 cycles, 430px wide).&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;Sequential Stalling&lt;/b&gt;: The &lt;i&gt;ROW_LOOP&lt;/i&gt; has &lt;b&gt;no overlap&lt;/b&gt;. The system wastes its memory bandwidth waiting for the 2.8M cycle compute engine to finish before loading the next row, confirming the need for Macro-Dataflow at the Top-Level." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#b85450;fillColor=#f8cecc;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;spacing=5;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
      <mxGeometry x="120" y="240" width="1300" height="60" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>

